  nonce: 89c4  # 89c4
  message: "C/C++ orphan rate (haproxy 29%): the orphan functions are primarily called via function pointers in dispatch tables and callback registrations. haproxy uses extensive macro-generated functions and struct-based callback dispatch (e.g., struct protocol has function pointer fields for .connect, .bind, .listen). Resolving these would require: (1) tracking assignments to struct function pointer fields, (2) resolving callback registration patterns. This is significant C analyzer work — not a quick fix."  # 89c4
