- op: discuss  # 4816
  at: '2026-03-19T02:06:58Z'  # 4816
  by: agent  # 4816
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4816
  clock: 4  # 4816
  nonce: '4816'  # 4816
  message: "C function pointer resolution requires tracking struct field assignments (e.g., protocol->connect = my_connect_func) and resolving indirect calls (ptr->connect()). This is a significant C analyzer feature that would benefit haproxy-style callback architectures. Recommend human decision: (A) implement struct-field function pointer tracking, (B) use heuristic matching (function name similarity), (C) accept as known limitation for callback-heavy C code."  # 4816
